From d11d90e6a9c2246abff95c23cfe2711575c836ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(images): two photo sets, seeded so 224 pages stop
 looking stamped
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both commissioned sets arrived complete — 37 files each, exact filenames,
exact dimensions, none over the size cap — and both hold the rule that makes
a comparison work. Checked frame by frame: in all twelve pairs across both
sets, flipping between before and after moves only the floor, the stair, the
rail or the deck. Same camera, same room, same light. Set B's install
"before" even carries chalk snap-lines on the subfloor.

That was the one thing code could not fix, and it is why all six services now
render as real comparisons instead of one pair and five stills.

The second set earns its keep somewhere specific. 224 of this site's 393
pages are service x city combinations and every one of them showed the
IDENTICAL staircase photograph — the strongest possible cue that the long
tail is one template stamped 224 times, however unique the words around it
are.

data/images.ts now picks between renditions deterministically, from a seed
the page already owns: the city slug on a matrix hero (13 of 32 cities draw
the second set), the service slug on a service hero, city+project on cards.
The estimator's comparison is seeded "estimator" and the service page's by
its slug, so a visitor who sees both sees two different jobs.

Deterministic, never random, for three reasons written out in the file: these
pages are prerendered and edge-cached, so a random pick would be frozen at
build time anyway; a server random and a client random disagree, which is a
hydration error; and a returning visitor should see the same page twice while
a different city looks different. Without a seed the canonical file comes
back unchanged, so every unseeded call site is byte-identical to before.

PhotoRotator crossfades the two renditions on exactly two dwell surfaces —
the showroom sample board and the workshop — under the same discipline as the
slider: both frames in the DOM from first render so there is no layout shift
and no mid-fade request, holds on hover, stops off-screen and in a hidden
tab, never starts under prefers-reduced-motion. Everywhere else the variant
is chosen once; a page whose images quietly swap themselves is unreadable.

These are still commissioned renderings. Holding a room fixed across a pair
makes the slider work; it does not make the images documentary. verified
stays false on all six, every frame renders under "Illustrative rendering,
not documentary job photography", and blocker #12 is unchanged.

SYNTHETIC_IMAGES is derived now rather than typed — 74 literals is a list
that goes stale on the next file added. It expands from the variant manifest,
so the day a real photograph lands it will not be in the set and
tests/images.test.ts fails with "the honesty guard has a hole", forcing a
deliberate decision instead of letting the guard quietly shrink.

The images themselves are not in this patch: 38 MB of binaries do not belong
in a diff, and both zips are already on main. scripts/install-image-sets.sh
installs them idempotently and was run from a clean checkout to prove it
reproduces the 74-file tree exactly.

338 tests pass (327 before), including an assertion that the 32 city slugs
actually spread across both renditions rather than all hashing the same way.
393 pages, audit clean, 8 routes x 4 viewports with no overflow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
